---
title: Chicken Biryiani in a Rice Cooker
servings: 6
course: dinner
tags: chicken, rice, one-pan
image: https://assets.afcdn.com/recipe/20100120/15385_w1024h1024c1cx192cy256.jpg
source: https://www.marmiton.org/recettes/recette_biryiani-de-poulet-en-rice-cooker_36787.aspx
prep time: 45m
cook time: 20m
---

The idea of this recipe is to prepare the different ingredients separately, then assemble them in successive layers before letting the rice cooker do the work!

Marinate the @chicken thigh{4}(cut into small pieces, salted) in the @garam masala{2%tbsp} and the @yoghurt{150%g}.

Then brown the @&chicken thigh{} in @butter{2%tbsp}(or ghee) in a #frying pan{}, add the @red onion{2}(sliced) and the @garlic clove{4}(crushed) and cook until browned.

Cook the @potato{3}(medium, diced) and the @carrot{2}(diced) in a #pot{} with a pinch of @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Place the meat first in the bottom of the #rice cooker{} bowl, then the vegetables, the @canned lentil{400%g}(cooked, drained), the raw @basmati rice{200%g} with the opened @cardamom pod{3}, and gently cover with @water{} and a pinch of @?red food colouring{}.

Press the button on the #rice cooker{}, which will switch off by itself, about ~{20%minutes}.

Garnish with the @egg{2}(hard-boiled)(cut into quarters) and the @coriander{}.
